{"skill": "Word Choice", "difficulty": "Medium", "question": "Throughout his extensive expeditions across Asia, Marco Polo not only encountered a multitude of diverse communities but also took careful notes on their customs, traditions, and daily life. His detailed travel writings offered Europe an unprecedented window into cultures that had been little known until then. By blending factual observation with thoughtful description, his accounts helped bridge cultural gaps and fostered a more nuanced understanding of distant societies. 

